# UX structure

## One main task per screen
- Each route has one primary action (one filled button). Everything else is secondary or moves away.
- Too much for one view? Split it: sub-routes (`/settings/profile`, `/settings/billing`),
  tabs for sibling views of the same thing, a drawer for details or quick edits, a stepper for long forms.
- Show the 3–5 things people need first; put the rest behind "More", a tab, or a detail page.
- Deep links: every tab, drawer and step has a URL, so Back and refresh work.

## Designed states, every time
- Loading: skeletons shaped like the real layout (no bare spinners on full pages, no layout jump).
- Empty: what will appear here + one action ("No invoices yet. Create your first invoice.").
- Error: plain cause + next step + retry; keep the user's input. Never a raw error or blank page.
- Also: partial data, offline/slow, no permission, success confirmation.

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)
- Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for text, ≥ 3:1 for large text, icons, borders of inputs and focus rings.
- Everything works by keyboard; visible focus that is never hidden behind sticky bars (2.4.11).
- Targets ≥ 24×24 px (2.5.8); no drag-only actions without a button alternative (2.5.7).
- Real elements: `<button>`, `<a href>`, `<label for>`, one `<h1>`, landmarks (`<main>`, `<nav>`).
- Icon-only buttons get `aria-label`; images get meaningful `alt` or `alt=""`.
- Errors are tied to fields (`aria-describedby`) and announced (`role="alert"` / live region).
- Don't ask for the same info twice (3.3.7); sign-in allows paste and password managers (3.3.8).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; nothing flashes.
- Add an axe check to e2e (see `~/.config/chigozie-rules/a11y.e2e.snippet.ts`); zero violations to merge.

## Must not look like an MVP
- One spacing scale, one type scale, consistent radii and shadows; align to a grid.
- Real copy, real icons, no lorem ipsum, no default browser alerts or unstyled tables.
- No dead ends: no "Coming soon" buttons, disabled controls explain why.

## Do / Don't
| Don't | Do |
| --- | --- |
| Settings page with 40 fields in one scroll | `/settings/profile`, `/settings/team`, `/settings/billing` |
| Order table + edit form + history on one screen | Table; row opens a drawer; history is a tab in the drawer |
| Spinner in the middle of a blank page | Skeleton rows matching the table |
| `<div onClick>` as a button | `<button type="button">` |
| Red border as the only error signal | Icon + text message linked with `aria-describedby` |
| Three primary buttons in a header | One primary, the rest as secondary or in a menu |
